A||||5||fieroshop||Buying parts||||1||
Z||000000||fieroshop||02-04-2000||01:17 AM||||I've been told that some of my parts are a little more expensive then some other people. The problem is that the other person is a person that has come across a Fiero or two and they decided that they would part it out. Granted their prices are and should be lower as they are not a bussines but a person just out to have some fun and help their Fiero friends. Fortunatly they don't have an overhead and can sell for very little. The bad part is I have an overhead and I have to pay wages. I have mechanics working for me and they and their family depend on my paying their wages. So not only do I have to pay them for dismanteling the Fieros I have in stock but I also have to pay  the government for all the licenses that goes in owning a shop and the lease of the property. I have overhead to worry about and that is how I and other shops make a living. For that reason our prices are higher and need to be in order to survive. I and other shops do not get upset if you can get parts from private parties. Just remember that buying from a shop you have much more recourse then buying from a private party.<p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 02-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-04-2000||04:00 AM||||I thought you just worked on Fieros.  My bad.  What kinds of parts do you sell?  I'd rather buy from a forum member (even if it costs a little more) than a non member.  I like to keep my business in the "family".   (That didn't sound quite right, but you know what I mean. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-04-2000||10:57 AM||||I think that most FieroNs know were to go to get a good deal on parts/services. That 100.00 part from a shop or parts store???? You can bay a parts car for 200.00-300.00 just as you do Fiero Shop, then you sell the other parts to friends/fourm members etc. Thats just part of fiero life. With fourms like this and clubs out there someone will always beat a shop/store price. Look at the price of that holley scoop????????||||reg||5
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||02-07-2000||11:20 AM||||Here's a good find: A friend of mine bought ANSA exhuast tips same sa FS, but he paid $40.00 for the set(2 tips) I've seen these for $80.00+ per set.  HOW?  He got them from a muffler shop that was going out of business. So if you have the $$$ and are in the right place at the right time this is what you can do. I told him that he should have bought all that they had at that price. He said that he wasn't thinking and had forgot about me and the fieros.   O well next time!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-07-2000||01:21 PM||||I like to do business with the Fiero Shops like yours and Ed Park's even if it costs a bit more.  If you guys go out of business we all lose out on your interest and expertise.  I mostly talk with Ed Parks because he is in my area.  He has always given his time to help me out with answering questions, etc.<P>The same goes for FOCOA.  If Phil decides that there isn't enough interest to be worth his time he'll fold up and be gone forever.  FOCOA has spent many thousands of dollars on tooling to have "no-longer-available' parts manufactured.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||02-07-2000||03:34 PM||||Yes we all like to help fieroNs But lets face it we all like to get a deal. Like I said with fourms like this and Fiero clubs you can always find a better price if you look. I have bought stuff from members here at a much lower price than shops/parts stores.<BR>I just bought seatcovers from a fourm member, they just came today, I can count it as one of the best buys I've got. He even sent the video, hog rings, and the hog ring tool.They are used but in very good shape. The passenger side looks new.<P>||||reg||14
